---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site.ts';
---

<Base
  title="Terms of use"
  description={`Rules for using ${site.name}: estimates only, no medical or electrical advice, manufacturer pages win on specs, and how to report a wrong number.`}
>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-12">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight md:text-4xl">Terms of use</h1>
    <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-ink-500 dark:text-ink-400">Last updated: {site.legalUpdated}.</p>

    <p class="mt-6 max-w-[68ch] text-ink-600 dark:text-ink-300">
      These terms apply to {site.name} at https://{site.domain} and to the calculator, scenario
      pages, station pages, and guides on that domain. They explain the intended use and limitations
      of the service. Nothing on this page overrides rights that applicable law does not allow us
      to exclude.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">What this site is</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-[68ch] text-ink-600 dark:text-ink-300">
      {site.name} is a free planning tool. It sizes a portable power station from a list of devices,
      and it republishes manufacturer specifications with a source URL and a verification date. It
      is not a store, not a licensed electrician, not a clinician, and not a laboratory.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Estimates, not a product</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-[68ch] text-ink-600 dark:text-ink-300">
      Runtime, recommended capacity, surge checks, and solar figures are planning estimates. They
      are calculated from published nameplate numbers and from engineering ranges in the device
      library. They move with temperature, battery age, inverter losses, duty cycle, and how your
      specific appliance actually draws power.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-[68ch] text-ink-600 dark:text-ink-300">
      An estimate is not a warranty, a test report, a certification, or a promise that a station
      will start or run your load. The
      <a class="text-moss-700 underline dark:text-moss-300" href="/methodology/">methodology page</a>
      describes the calculation. If a displayed result conflicts with the documented method, do
      not rely on it. Contact us so we can investigate; either the code or the description may be
      wrong.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Not medical advice</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-[68ch] text-ink-600 dark:text-ink-300">
      A portable power station is not a medical device. It is not a substitute for the battery
      module your equipment manufacturer specifies for a CPAP, BiPAP, concentrator, or any other
      therapy device. Pages that mention CPAP are watt-hour estimates. They are not a therapy plan
      and they are not a compatibility rating.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-[68ch] text-ink-600 dark:text-ink-300">
      If you depend on a therapy device, confirm the backup plan with your equipment provider and
      your clinician before an outage. Do not treat a number on this site as clearance to skip that
      conversation.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Not electrical advice</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-[68ch] text-ink-600 dark:text-ink-300">
      Never backfeed household wiring through a wall or dryer outlet. This can create a fatal shock
      hazard. Whole-home backup needs a manufacturer-approved, code-compliant transfer or isolation
      system, installed by a qualified electrician where required. Do not connect to household
      circuits without that system. Follow the equipment instructions for direct appliance use.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-[68ch] text-ink-600 dark:text-ink-300">
      A "solar generator" on this site means a battery with an optional solar input. It does not
      generate electricity on its own. Without panels it only holds what you charge into it.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Specifications</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-[68ch] text-ink-600 dark:text-ink-300">
      Capacity, continuous watts, peak watts, and other station fields are copied from the
      manufacturer page named on the model record, with a verification date. If the manufacturer
      page and this site disagree, the manufacturer page wins. Manufacturers change pages. A figure
      verified more than 90 days ago is flagged on the model page for that reason.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-[68ch] text-ink-600 dark:text-ink-300">
      Some peak figures are resistive boost ratings (for example X-Boost or Power Lifting), not
      inverter surge. Those records are marked so a motor start is not treated as cleared. Device
      wattages in the picker are typical ranges, not a measurement of your machine.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-[68ch] text-ink-600 dark:text-ink-300">
      If a number here is wrong, email the model name and the manufacturer URL that contradicts us
      to
      <!--email_off--><a class="text-moss-700 underline dark:text-moss-300" href={`mailto:${site.contactEmail}`}>{site.contactEmail}</a><!--/email_off-->.
      We will investigate and update confirmed errors. Reporting a correction does not limit any
      legal rights or remedies you may have.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Your load data</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-[68ch] text-ink-600 dark:text-ink-300">
      The calculator runs in your browser. A shared URL can be read by anyone who has the link. See
      the <a class="underline" href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a>.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Acceptable use</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-[68ch] text-ink-600 dark:text-ink-300">
      You may use the calculator and read the pages for personal planning. You may not:
    </p>
    <ul class="mt-4 space-y-3 text-sm text-ink-600 dark:text-ink-300">
      <li class="max-w-[68ch]">Scrape the catalog to republish it as your own verified database.</li>
      <li class="max-w-[68ch]">Present this site's estimates to someone else as medical or electrical advice from us.</li>
      <li class="max-w-[68ch]">Overload, deface, impersonate, or attempt to break the site.</li>
      <li class="max-w-[68ch]">Use automated traffic that is meant to distort Analytics or to copy the database.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Intellectual property</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-[68ch] text-ink-600 dark:text-ink-300">
      The calculator, the copy, and the arrangement of the spec library are {site.name}. Brand
      names, model names, and packshots belong to their manufacturers. They appear here to identify
      products, not as an endorsement by those manufacturers.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Third-party sites</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-[68ch] text-ink-600 dark:text-ink-300">
      Manufacturer source links leave this site. Their terms and privacy rules apply once you are
      there. Until affiliate programs are live, those links are source citations, not checkout.
      Status is on the
      <a class="underline" href="/disclosure/">affiliate disclosure</a>.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">No warranty</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-[68ch] text-ink-600 dark:text-ink-300">
      To the extent permitted by applicable law, the site is provided as is and as available.
      {site.name} does not warrant that a figure is
      current, that a station will start a given load, or that the service will be uninterrupted.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Limitation of liability</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-[68ch] text-ink-600 dark:text-ink-300">
      These estimates cannot account for every device, installation, or outage. Verify equipment
      requirements before making purchase or backup decisions. To the extent permitted by
      applicable law, we exclude liability for indirect or consequential losses arising from use
      of this free planning tool.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-[68ch] text-ink-600 dark:text-ink-300">
      Nothing in these terms excludes or limits liability that cannot lawfully be excluded or
      limited, including liability for fraud or for death or personal injury caused by negligence
      where applicable law prohibits that exclusion. Statutory consumer rights and non-excludable
      remedies remain unaffected.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Changes</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-[68ch] text-ink-600 dark:text-ink-300">
      These terms may be updated when the service changes. The date at the top identifies the
      published version. Changes do not remove non-excludable rights or apply retroactively where
      applicable law prohibits that.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Contact</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-[68ch] text-ink-600 dark:text-ink-300">
      {site.name}, {site.domain}. Email
      <!--email_off--><a class="text-moss-700 underline dark:text-moss-300" href={`mailto:${site.contactEmail}`}>{site.contactEmail}</a><!--/email_off-->.
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>
